0,Baga language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baga_language,"Most Baga are bilingual in the Mande language Susu, the official regional language. Two ethnically Baga communities, Sobané and Kaloum, are known to have abandoned their language altogether in favour of Susu.",Baga Kaloum,Niger-Congo
1,Baga Kaloum jezik – Wikipedija,https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baga_Kaloum_jezik,"Baga kaloum je jedan od dva izumrla baga jezika, a na tom putu je i treći jezik baga koga, a pripadnici etničkih skupina prihvatili su jezik susu, predstavnika skupine mande.",Baga Kaloum,Niger-Congo
2,Baga Kaloum is an extinct language of Guinea. It belongs to the Niger...,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bqf/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..t8CyCLwjEiJt5OrRWjMTuJ4hhLLKH2Xrk4eTyMP_At4,It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family.This graph shows the vitality of Baga Kaloum. Institutional — The language has been developed to the point that it is used and sustained by institutions beyond the home and community.,Baga Kaloum,Niger-Congo
